{:id :EACL-FORMAL-064
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :benchmark
 :seed-or-trace
 "datascript/content-proof/lookup-page/cache-bypass/relationship-width"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :performance
 :affected-versions
 ["v8.0 commit e50f1cb5395e105edf3875d50e0afb16b1ba7cee"]
 :affected-backends [:datascript]
 :root-cause
 "Cursor construction always supplied the permission relation closure. In default content-proof mode the DataScript adapter converted that request into a full relationship-content digest, so even a cache-bypassed seven-item demand page scanned the entire authorization graph merely to mint its cursor."
 :fix
 "Supply dependency relation ids only for explicit managed mutation-stamp mode. Default content/no-proof modes bind exact immutable snapshot identity; current-only DataScript rejects every later basis instead of scanning content or yielding a hybrid page."
 :closing-evidence
 ["PageWindow.ContentCursorMintingDoesNoRelationProofScan"
  "PageWindow.OnlyManagedMutationModeRequestsDependencyProof"
  "PageWindow.DataScriptChangedBasisCannotYieldCursorPage"
  "eacl.datascript.enumeration-routing-test/content-proof-cursors-use-current-basis-without-relation-scan-test"
  "eacl.bench.explorer-enumeration-test/explorer-10000-user-page-does-not-scale-with-denotation"]}
